  "articleSummary": "The article argues that search is a broad discipline and that semantic/vector search should complement—not replace—exact-match, lexical, and fuzzy search in a hybrid architecture. It explains embeddings, vectors, lexical search, semantic similarity, and BM25, then compares 16 technologies—including pgvector, Qdrant, Weaviate, Pinecone, Milvus, Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, Vespa, and others—by deployment, licensing, capabilities, and workload fit. The tone is practical and analytical with a tutorial-like emphasis on choosing the right tool rather than “embedding everything.” Its intended audience is engineers and technical decision-makers who need to design, evaluate, and clearly justify search systems.",
